        "evidence": [
          {
            "page": 1,
            "section": "Abstract",
            "quote": "we derive an information limit: if executions with identical policy-visible fields require different effect-specific decisions, no deterministic or randomized record-only policy can guarantee both."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "claim": "Binding frozen, source-backed predictions before authorization cuts residual effect instances from 10 to 3 on 17 target-executed workflows.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "page": 2,
